<title>UK: Smithkline says stg has &quot;dramatic impact&quot;.</title>
<headline>Smithkline says stg has &quot;dramatic impact&quot;.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Anglo-U.S. drugs group SmithKline Beecham Plc said on Tuesday that sterling's strength against other European currencies and against the dollar had a &quot;dramatic impact&quot; in the first quarter of 1997.</p>
<p>Pre-tax profit rose by 19 percent at constant exchange rates to 459 million stg, but the stronger pound reduced actual growth to 8 percent, giving a figure of 418 million stg.</p>
<p>Underlying sales rose 7 percent, but on a headline basis, overall sales fell 2 percent to 1.84 billion stg.</p>
</text>
